Pulso uses the accompaniment, bass, vocal and drum estimators, converted to ONNX and
quantized to int8. They retain input frequencies up to 16 kHz and output the
first 1116 frequency bins (approximately 12 kHz), sufficient for charting.
The application reconstructs separated instrumental audio in memory for transcription.

